# cspell:words precompiler closurizing closurized tearoff selfhost
#
# Dispatch-table fixes that let a Flutter app COMPILE AND RUN on our
# vanilla-Dart engine. Apply to engine/src/flutter/third_party/dart.
#
# Two rules, both from language semantics rather than from metadata:
#
#   1. Only a REGULAR method can be torn off, so only a regular method may get
#      a method extractor here. Dart has no tear-off of a getter or a setter,
#      and a setter's ProcedureAttributes.getter_selector_id names its FIELD'S
#      getter — `_selectorIdForMember` keys `_getterMemberIds` by a Kernel
#      `Name`, which does not distinguish setters. Letting one through wrote
#      the extractor for `set:_data` into `get:_data`'s row.
#   2. A tear-off row belongs only to a genuinely distinct getter selector.
#      `getter_selector_id` can be the method's own id (Object.get:hashCode is
#      one), and writing there displaces the method itself.
#
# Everything metadata-shaped that used to live here — the IsUsed() removals and
# the torn_off bypass — is GONE as of 2026-08-05. Those were compensating for a
# forked frontend_server's dill being read by this vanilla backend; the fix was
# to ship a matching frontend. See selfhost/TFA_ROOT_CAUSE.md.
